## Template locations and metadata

- All AI-driven templates live in `.ai_content/.ai_templates/`.
- Each template begins with YAML front matter describing:
  - `id`: unique identifier
  - `vars`: list of `${VAR}` placeholders to fill
  - `out`: output path under `.ai_content/.ai_docs/`

## Rendering workflow

1) Parse the front matter.
2) Resolve variables (highest → lowest precedence):
   - Existing rendered doc in `.ai_content/.ai_docs/` relevant to the request
   - Repository context (branch name, diff, history)
   - Current platform issue/PR context
   - Ask for any still-missing variables
3) Replace all `${VAR}` placeholders in the body (no loops/conditionals).
4) Write output to the `out` path, preserving subdirectories (create dirs if needed).

## Guardrails

- Do not hallucinate values. Ask for missing ones.
- Do not invent facts not present in code, diff, or linked items.
- Keep outputs within the repository unless explicitly instructed to post to a platform UI.

## Common template mappings

- PR body → `.ai_content/.ai_templates/pr/default.tpl.md`
- Issue body → `.ai_content/.ai_templates/issue/feature.tpl.md`
- Commit message → `.ai_content/.ai_templates/commit/conventional.tpl.txt`
